# An allowlist: everything is excluded, and a file ships only when a line below names it. A new
# file in the repository therefore stays out of the package until someone decides otherwise.
#
# Every pattern is anchored at the repository root, so a worktree under .claude/worktrees stays out
# whole: its own package.json, node_modules and bundles match none of the lines below.
#
# vsce applies a negation after every ignore pattern, whatever the order of the lines, so the
# sections below can grow independently.
**

# The extension manifest, and the listing pages vsce builds from these files.
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE

# The declaration both the client and the model server read at run time, from this location.
!capabilities.json

# The client bundle. It includes vscode-languageclient, so nothing beside it is needed.
!client/dist/extension.js

# The model server bundle, and the manifest beside it. The manifest gives the bundle its
# `"type": "module"` and is what the server reads to answer idfkit-lsp/versions.
!model-server/dist/main.js
!model-server/package.json

# The bundle leaves @idfkit/* external and @idfkit/schemas is read from disk, so those packages must
# sit in model-server/node_modules at run time. Every other package there is bundled or dev only.
!model-server/node_modules/@idfkit/**

# Deliberately absent:
# - server/: the source server is installed with pip and started as `python -m idfkit_lsp`.
# - levels.json: read by the repository's checks and bump workflows, and by nothing at run time.
# - dist/*.map: no runtime here loads them, and they weigh more than the bundles they describe.
